"memory": "Round 1: Initial task. I own normalize.js. Must implement normalize(text): NFKC, lowercase, collapse whitespace to single ASCII space, trim. Only for string input; otherwise behavior unspecified but should be safe (return input as-is? Spec says 'for string input' so non-string can return as-is). No shadowing injected normalize/tokenize. Peers: tokenizer calls normalize, pipeline calls tokenize. Next rounds may refine edge cases. Keep implementation simple, faithful, no extras.",
"files": {
"normalize.js": "function normalize(text) {
  if (typeof text !== 'string') {
    return text;
  }
  // NFKC normalization via String.prototype.normalize (available in QuickJS).
  var normalized = text.normalize('NFKC');
  // Lowercase.
  normalized = normalized.toLowerCase();
  // Collapse whitespace to one ASCII space, then trim.
  normalized = normalized.replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim();
  return normalized;
}
"
